		<title type="html"><![CDATA[New Beta 2023 11 19]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3497&amp;p=27538#p27538"><![CDATA[
A new Beta version is available for the MD9600/RT90<br><br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/Latest</a><br><br><br>Changes since the last Beta release are<br><br>Firmware:<ul><li> VOX bugfixes.</li><li> Don't trigger the vox when VP is playing.</li><li> Various languages updates.</li><li> GPS NMEA logging added (optional). <ul> <li> NMEA log clearing at boot time (SK1 + 5, and front DOWN + 5 n MD-9600, undocumented).</li> <li> using Logging on &lt; 16Mb devices disable the DMDId feature (cleared).</li> </ul></li><li> APRS beaconing added (Channel/VFO/Satellite). <ul> <li> please refer to the user guide for details.</li> </ul></li><li> Satellite: Voice/APRS/CW Rx modes added..</li><li> Show/Sort distance to repeater feature added.</li><li> VP updated.</li><li> Ability to read and write calibration data on STM32 platform (needs the latest CPS).</li><li> Fix menu system bug (cancelation/validation on Options ones).</li><li> Fix problems with CPS communication when the GPS NMEA output is enabled.</li><li> Ability to save the secure registers using the CPS on STM32 devices.</li><li> Fix a CWID bug in the hotspot mode.</li><li> Adds Auto Lock options (see the user guide).</li><li> Various bugfixes.</li></ul><br>This version features the APRS beacon functionality described in this post  <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=16&amp;t=3352&amp;start=10#p26717" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=16&amp;t=3352&amp;start=10#p26717</a>  <br><br>Thanks to Daniel F1RMB for the majority of these new features and bug fixes and to Colin G4EML <br>The User Guide will be fully updated to document all the new features soon.<br><br><br>Note. <br><br>Existing voice prompt files do not work with this version. The latest new versions can be downloaded from here<br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest</a><br><br>Also the functionality to read and write the calibration data requires the latest CPS, which can be downloaded from here<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/PC_CPS/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/PC_CPS/Latest</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Nov 19, 2023 10:19 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
